    "Fix treats only float32-scale boundary roundoff as clipped_detection (zero on both axes); real out-of-frame geometry, stale frames, and ambiguity still stop as before.",
    "Historical logs lack boxes and candidate counts: the rounding defect is reproduced in software but is not proven to explain each historical invalid_detection. Ambiguity may be multiple people or detector false positives; cannot distinguish from retained logs.",
    "Added bounded incoming-frame diagnostics including rejected timestamps, source age, receipt gap, box geometry and candidate counts; preserve first latched fault.",
    "External dependency commits match portable_hri.repos. HRI prefixes resolve to this workspace after sourcing install/setup.bash. Source and installed app scripts are linked.",
